  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the probability of the maximum outcome in each lottery. In this case, Lottery A has a higher probability (100%) of its maximum outcome (2400) than Lottery B has of its maximum outcome (33% for 2500). The individual does consider probabilities and outcomes, but the justification is not based on the probability of the maximum outcome per se. Instead, the individual emphasizes certainty, risk aversion, and the small gain relative to the risk of getting nothing. There is no mention of 'maximum outcome' or comparing probabilities of best possible results. The reasoning is more aligned with risk aversion or certainty effect rather than the specific rule of maximizing the probability of the maximum outcome. Therefore, while the conclusion aligns with the decision reason (choosing A), the underlying justification differs in logic.",
  "final_assessment_score": 30
