  "step_2": "The individual reports considering the sums (outcomes) and their associated probabilities. They first mention using expected value as a criterion ('die lotterie die die höhere erwartete auszahlung hat'), but then note that the expected values are equal (which is correct: both lotteries have an expected value of 0 Euros). Subsequently, they justify their choice with the statement 'besser nichts als chance auf verlust' (better nothing than a chance of loss), indicating a preference for certainty and aversion to the risk of loss, even when expected values are equal. The individual thus shifts from expected value to a risk-averse, certainty-based justification.",
